Agar video public ho gayi lekin baad mein claim aa gaya ya koi issue nikla, to system ye automatically karega:

#### 1. Automated Post-Public Monitoring (Weekly Re-Scan)
Content ID dynamic hota hai. Jo video aaj safe hai, wo kal claim ho sakti hai agar owner ne naya fingerprint add kiya.
*   **Logic:** Har hafte published videos ki list fetch karo → `videos.list` se unka status check karo.
*   **Action:** Agar naya claim detect hua:
    *   *Audio Claim:* Auto-mute segment via YouTube Editor API.
    *   *Visual Claim:* Video ko turant `UNLISTED` karo aur rerender queue mein daalo.
    *   *Block >20%:* Video ko `PRIVATE` karo aur log generate karo.

#### 2. Emergency Fallback Protocol (2 Options)
Jab public video par problem aaye, to ye decision tree follow karein:

| Scenario | Auto-Action | Manual Override Option |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Music/Audio Claim** | Replace with YT Audio Library track | Accept Revenue Share (if monetized) |
| **Visual Segment Claim** | Trim claimed part via Editor API | Dispute (only if Fair Use valid) |
| **Full Block / Strike Risk** | Set to PRIVATE immediately | Delete permanently |
| **False Positive** | File dispute with template | Contact rights holder directly |

#### 3. Self-Healing Rerender Loop
Agar post-public claim aata hai:
1.  Video ko auto-unlisted/private karo.
2.  Original source file se **stricter filters** (more zoom, different BGM) laga kar naya version render karo.
3.  Naye version ko phir se Unlisted Buffer se guzaro.
4.  Safe hone par purane video ko delete karke naya public karo.

